msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/incomplete-designs.md:23
msgid "_Declared_, _open_ and _not applied_ are the intentional states. They are drawn in orange, with dashes or hollow — never red. Red is reserved for _wrong now_."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/incomplete-designs.md:26
msgid "The states of a design"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/incomplete-designs.md:28
msgid "A whole design is **executable** when every relationship an output depends on is valid and every required output has exactly one driver. Below that, the status line at the bottom of the window tells you what is still open, as counts and short phrases: _2 not yet defined_, _outputs incomplete_, _not causal_, _reads across domains_."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/incomplete-designs.md:34
msgid "The Simulate page turns the same facts into sentences with links: _tilt needs a value before simulation can step._ — _dimByTilt has no definition._ — _level has no valid definition._ Each _Show_ link selects the object. Nothing here is a failure; it is the list of what remains. Below those, with a hollow dot, the notes that stop nothing but explain the trace: _dimByTilt is a rule nothing applies yet._, with the fix that writes the value applying it."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/incomplete-designs.md:41
msgid "Why BDL is built this way"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/incomplete-designs.md:43
msgid "Design is discovered in an order that does not match the order of dependency. You know the lamp will have a light before you know the formula; you know a relationship reads _Temperature_ before you know whether temperature is a quantity in kelvin or a coarse _cold / warm / hot_. A tool that refused to hold the design until every piece was decided would push you back to sketches. BDL holds the design, checks the parts that can be checked, and reports the rest as _open_ — with the same precision it uses for errors, so that \"what is left\" is always a concrete list."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/incomplete-designs.md:52
msgid "The practical consequences:"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/incomplete-designs.md:54
msgid "A relationship without inputs and without a formula is a **Source**, not a declared one: it is exactly what the simulator asks you for. A sensor reading is a Source with a domain. \"Comes from the environment\" is a complete state, on purpose; give the Source a formula and it becomes a computed value instead."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/incomplete-designs.md:58
msgid "An **open** relationship does not turn red when you change the concept it waits on; it is re-checked and becomes valid or invalid."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/incomplete-designs.md:60
msgid "An **undriven** required output is _incomplete_, an **undriven optional** output is fine, and a **contested** output (two drivers) is an error — because the first two are missing information and the third is a contradiction."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/incomplete-designs.md:64
msgid "Finishing a design"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/incomplete-designs.md:66
msgid "The Simulate page's list, the status line, and the **Fixes** section of an inspector all point at the same work. Fixes are actions the tool can offer for a finding — _Choose what Temperature is represented by_, _Connect a driver to light_, _Add a value that applies dimByTilt_ — each applied as an ordinary edit you can undo. A fix is ready when the tool can do it alone, a pop-up when you must choose, and a sentence saying why when it cannot be done yet; it never guesses."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/incomplete-designs.md:76
msgid "_For language implementers._ The kernel treats a declaration without a realization as a legal, unresolved declaration; the ladder a mapping climbs is _Declared → Open → Invalid → TypeValid → TemporallyValid → ClockConsistent_, and output completeness and hardware feasibility are properties of the design and of a (design, target) pair, not rungs. `docs/architecture/compiler-pipeline.md` (\"Driver and result\") and ADR-0015."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/incomplete-designs.md:85
msgid "[Relationships](relationships.md) · [Status meanings](../reference/status-meanings.md) · [Troubleshooting: incomplete design](../troubleshooting/incomplete-design.md)"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:1
msgid "Physical outputs"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:3
msgid "A **physical output** is where a value leaves the design for the world: a light, a motor, a display, a buzzer. It is not a concept and not a relationship. It **accepts** one concept, **updates in** one timing domain, and is **driven** by exactly one value of the design."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:8
msgid "Do not confuse it with a relationship's _output_ — the concept a relationship produces. `dimByTilt` produces _Brightness_; _light_ is a physical output that accepts _Brightness_. The first is a meaning inside the design; the second is the lamp."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:13
msgid "The rules, in designer terms"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:15
msgid "Rule"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:15
msgid "Why"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:17
msgid "An output accepts **one concept**."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:17
msgid "The lamp shows a brightness, not \"a number\". Connecting an _Opacity_ would be a mistake the tool can catch."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:18
msgid "An output has **one timing domain**, and its driver must update in that domain."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:18
msgid "The physical device refreshes at the domain's rhythm; a driver on another rhythm would leave the output reading a value from an unrelated instant."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:19
msgid "An output is driven by a **value** — a relationship that reads nothing."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:19
msgid "A rule is something you apply; only a value can be _the_ brightness at this tick. `brightness = dimByTilt(tilt)` drives; `dimByTilt` cannot. Studio offers the connection only to values."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:20
msgid "An output has **at most one driver**."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:20
msgid "Two relationships driving one light is a contradiction in the design. BDL names it and does not pick a winner — no priorities, no last-writer. Combine the two values in a relationship and connect that."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:21
msgid "A **required** output must be driven for the design to be executable; an optional one may stay undriven."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:21
msgid "A lamp without its light is unfinished; an optional status LED is not."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:23
msgid "The states of an output"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:25
#: docs/user-guide/reference/formula-language.md:53
#: docs/user-guide/reference/status-meanings.md:9
#: docs/user-guide/reference/status-meanings.md:28
#: docs/user-guide/reference/status-meanings.md:44
#: docs/user-guide/reference/status-meanings.md:55
#: docs/user-guide/reference/status-meanings.md:66
#: docs/user-guide/reference/status-meanings.md:74
#: docs/user-guide/reference/status-meanings.md:83
#: docs/user-guide/reference/terminology.md:8
#: docs/user-guide/studio/deploy.md:56
#: docs/user-guide/troubleshooting/connection-errors.md:116
msgid "Meaning"
msgstr "含义"

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:27
msgid "dashed sink, _no timing domain yet_"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:27
msgid "the output exists but has no domain; nothing can drive it yet and nothing is wrong"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:28
msgid "**undriven**"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:28
msgid "dashed sink; inspector: _Undriven — the design is incomplete without a driver._ (required) or _Undriven._ (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:28
msgid "waiting for a driver"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:29
msgid "**driven**"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:29
msgid "solid sink; _Driven by brightness._"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:29
msgid "complete"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:30
msgid "**ill-formed**"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:30
msgid "the sink shows the word _ill-formed_; the driver carries a finding: wrong concept, wrong domain, or a rule with inputs"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:30
msgid "the connection was recorded, and it is wrong"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:31
#: docs/user-guide/reference/terminology.md:35
msgid "**contested**"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:31
msgid "the sink shows the word _contested_; inspector lists every claimant"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:31
msgid "two or more drivers"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:33
msgid "Findings about a connection belong to the _connection_: the driving relationship itself stays valid, and the finding appears under that relationship's **Drives** section and under the output's **Driver** section."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:37
#: docs/user-guide/reference/status-meanings.md:7
msgid "On the canvas"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:39
msgid "An output is a **sink node** at the right edge of the canvas: a boundary bar and one input socket in the accepted concept's colour. Drag from a value's output socket onto the sink to connect; drag the link away from the sink and release on empty canvas to disconnect. Only a relationship's output socket can land on a sink; a concept row cannot drive the world by itself, and nothing reads from a sink."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:46
msgid "In the inspector"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:48
msgid "**Meaning** — name and description."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:49
msgid "**Output** — _Accepts_ (the concept), _Updates in_, _Required_."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:50
msgid "**Driver** — the state line, the claimants with _disconnect_ links, and a **Connect** pop-up listing the design's values of the accepted concept. When there is none, one sentence says so instead — _No value of Brightness in the design yet — a relationship that reads nothing and produces Brightness could drive this output._"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:55
msgid "**Fixes** — for a contested output, _Detach … from …_ and _Create upstream combination mapping_; for an undriven one, _Connect a driver to …_ with a choice."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:59
msgid "On a relationship's own page, the **Drives** section offers an _Output_ pop-up to a value only. A rule shows the caption _A rule cannot drive an output — connect the value that applies this rule._ and, when exactly one value of the design applies it, names that value with a _Show_ link. A text-authored design may still write a rule as a driver; then the connection is recorded, the finding appears under _Drives_ and _Driver_, and _Disconnect_ removes it."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:66
msgid "From output to device"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:68
msgid "Which piece of hardware realises an output — a PWM channel, a digital output, an H-bridge — is not part of the design. It is a **device** binding, edited on the Deploy page, and the board it is placed on is a per-session choice. Changing either never changes the design's verdicts. See [Deploy](../studio/deploy.md)."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:75
msgid "_For language implementers._ An output is an entry of `Ω` with an `OutputSpec { accepts, clock }`; a drive edge is `β d = o`. The well-formedness of a drive (`DriveWF`: exact type view and exact domain), the single-driver rule (`SingleDriver`) and completeness (`CompleteOutputs`) are checked by `bdl-output` after the semantic passes and never move a mapping down the status ladder (ADR-0015). `docs/guides/deployment-walkthrough.md` follows one value from a relationship to a pin. DI-20 records why only nullary relationships drive."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/physical-outputs.md:86
msgid "[Relationships](relationships.md) · [Timing](timing.md) · [Deploy](../studio/deploy.md) · [Troubleshooting: connections](../troubleshooting/connection-errors.md)"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:1
#: docs/user-guide/textual/syntax-basics.md:45
msgid "Relationships"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:3
msgid "A **relationship** says how one concept follows from others. `dimByTilt` reads _Tilt_ and produces _Brightness_; `adaptBrightness` reads _Brightness_ and _Ambient light_ and produces _Brightness_. A relationship has a name, a **signature** — the concepts it _reads_ and the one it _produces_ — and, once you write it, a **formula**."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:9
msgid "In the sidebar and the creation sheet, relationships are labelled _Mappings_. Same thing."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:12
msgid "Signature first, formula second"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:14
msgid "Creating a relationship only fixes its signature. That is enough for the rest of the design to be built around it: other relationships can apply it, an output can wait for it, the simulator can list what it still needs. The formula comes when you are ready, in the inspector's _Relationship_ section. Until then a relationship that reads something is dashed and _declared_; one that reads nothing is a **Source** — complete as it is, provided by the environment."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:21
msgid "The formula is checked against the signature as you type, and the check is in your own terms: _Brightness is a dimensionless quantity, but this formula produces an angle._"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:25
msgid "Three shapes of relationship"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:27
msgid "Shape"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:27
msgid "Reads"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:27
#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:197
msgid "Formula"
msgstr "公式"

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:27
msgid "What it is"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:29
msgid "**Rule**"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:29
msgid "one or more concepts"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:29
#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:31
#: docs/user-guide/textual/syntax-basics.md:162
#: docs/user-guide/textual/syntax-basics.md:163
#: docs/user-guide/textual/syntax-basics.md:164
#: docs/user-guide/textual/syntax-basics.md:165
#: docs/user-guide/textual/syntax-basics.md:167
#: docs/user-guide/textual/syntax-basics.md:168
#: docs/user-guide/textual/syntax-basics.md:169
msgid "yes"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:29
msgid "a function from concepts to a concept: `dimByTilt : Tilt → Brightness = Tilt / 90 deg`"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:30
#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:31
msgid "nothing"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:30
msgid "none"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:30
msgid "a value the environment provides — from a sensor, a switch, an analog line. In simulation you type it; on a device the hardware supplies it"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:31
msgid "**Computed value**"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:31
msgid "a value of the design: `brightness = dimByTilt(tilt)`"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:33
msgid "Only a relationship that _reads nothing_ is a value; a rule is something you apply. This matters in three places: a physical output can only be driven by a value; a formula applies a rule by calling it — `dimByTilt(tilt)` — and names a value by writing it — `tilt`; and only a value or a Source gives its concept a value at each tick. A rule _produces_ its concept in the sense of its signature — its output socket is that concept — but the concept is **carried** only by a value whose formula applies the rule. Until `brightness` exists, `dimByTilt` is a function nobody calls, and nothing carries _Brightness_."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:42
msgid "The creation sheet says which shape you are about to make as you change the reads: with nothing read, _Reads nothing: a Source…_; with something read, _Reads Tilt: a rule, a function to Brightness. It has no value of its own — a value's formula applies it…_. A computed value is a Source you then give a formula."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:48
msgid "Only a value shows in the simulator: a rule has no value per tick, so it has no column in the trace. A rule that nothing applies is a legal state, and the tool says so: the finding _dimByTilt is a rule nothing applies yet._ on the rule, in the inspector's _Relationship_ section and on the Simulate page, with the fix **Add a value that applies dimByTilt** — which creates `dimByTiltValue : () -> Brightness = dimByTilt(tilt)` when exactly one value produces each concept the rule reads, asks you to choose when several do, and says why when none does. On the canvas the rule's output socket is hollow — no value comes out of it yet — and, once the rule has a formula, its header reads _not applied_ instead of _rule_. It is not an error: nothing is wrong, something is still to be written."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:60
msgid "The formula"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:62
msgid "Formulas are short expressions over the names in scope: the concepts the relationship reads, the values and rules of the design, numbers with units, and a few keywords."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:73
msgid "A formula is checked for **dimension** (units must work out), for **meaning** (the result must be the concept the signature promises), and for **shape** (a rule cannot be used where a value is expected, and the other way round). The full language — operators, `if`, `let`, `match`, memory with `delay`, values from other domains with `sync` — is in [Formula language](../reference/formula-language.md); the editor is described in [Formula editor](../studio/formula-editor.md)."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:81
msgid "Links on the canvas"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:83
msgid "Two kinds of link, told apart by colour and by where they end. A link in a concept's colour from a concept's output socket to a relationship's input socket means _this relationship reads that concept_; from a relationship's output socket to a concept's input socket, _this relationship produces that concept_. These are the **signature**: drawing one edits it; dragging one away from an input and dropping it on empty canvas removes the concept from the signature. A thin grey link from a relationship's output socket to the left end of another relationship's formula line means _that formula names this relationship_ — `brightness`'s line receives one from `dimByTilt` (applied) and one from `tilt` (named). These are the **dependency**, read off the analysis of the formula; they follow the formula and cannot be dragged. On the canvas a rule wears the word _rule_ in its header; a value wears no word. Neither kind of link shows the arithmetic or an order of execution: the canvas is a picture of the interface and of dependency, not a flowchart."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:100
msgid "**Meaning** — name, description and _Role_: _Source_, _Rule_ or _Value_ (or the port the relationship backs), with one sentence."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:102
msgid "**Reads** / **Produces** — the signature, as chips and a pop-up with the concepts' glyphs. Changing either is an edit; the inspector says which relationships will be rechecked."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:105
msgid "**Relationship** — the formula editor: _Add definition_ / _Save definition_ / _Revert_ / _Detach definition_, the verdict line, and any findings about the formula; then _Depends on_ (the relationships the formula names) and _Named in_ (the formulas that name this one) — the reference links, as names you can click; then the findings about the relationship's place in the design — a rule nothing applies, with its fix beside it."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:111
msgid "**Timing** — _Updates in_: the timing domain, or _Any timing domain_ for a pure rule. See [Timing](timing.md)."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:113
msgid "**Drives** — the physical output this value is the final target of, if any. See [Physical outputs](physical-outputs.md)."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:115
msgid "**Fixes** — actions the tool offers for findings on this relationship."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:116
msgid "**Explain** — collapsed by default: the formal detail."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:120
msgid "_For language implementers._ A relationship is a declaration with an interface (the signature elaborated over the concepts' representations) and an optional realization (the formula elaborated to a Core term, a lambda over `rep` of each input ending in `mk` of the output). A declaration without a realization is the language's unresolved declaration, a first-class state. `docs/architecture/compiler-pipeline.md` passes 3–6; `docs/spec/textual-syntax.md` §11 for what elaborates; ADR-0013 for the formula language's naming rule. The reference links are the kernel's `dependsOn` (`docs/spec/kernel.md` §5) — `refs` of the realization, carried per relationship in the analysis (`MappingAnalysis.references`, ADR-0034)."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/relationships.md:133
msgid "[Concepts](concepts.md) · [Incomplete designs](incomplete-designs.md) · [Formula editor](../studio/formula-editor.md) · [Formula language](../reference/formula-language.md) · [Simulate](../studio/simulate.md)"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/timing.md:1
#: docs/user-guide/troubleshooting/timing-errors.md:1
msgid "Timing"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/timing.md:3
msgid "A product's values do not all move together. A touch sensor reports many times a second; a temperature sensor a few times a minute; a button when it is pressed. BDL makes those rhythms explicit, so that \"when does this update\" is a decision you can see, simulate and be warned about — not something that falls out of the firmware's loop order."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/timing.md:9
msgid "This page starts from the questions a designer asks and arrives at the three words the tool uses: **timing domain**, **delay**, **sync**."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/timing.md:12
msgid "How often does this sensor update?"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/timing.md:14
msgid "Every value that updates on its own — a sensor reading, a computed value that should refresh with it — belongs to a named **timing domain**. In the lamp, `tilt` and `brightness` both _update in_ **interaction**."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/timing.md:18
msgid "A domain is a **name**, not a rate. It says _these values tick together_; it does not say how often. How often is a property of the simulation (the period per domain on the Simulate page) or of the device, not of the design. Two domains with the same period are still two domains."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/timing.md:23
msgid "Create domains in the sidebar (**+** by _Timing domains_), assign them in a relationship's or output's inspector under **Timing › Updates in**. The domain's name is shown quietly at the right edge of the node."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/timing.md:27
msgid "When does this relationship run?"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/timing.md:29
msgid "A **rule** — a relationship with inputs, like `dimByTilt` — has no rhythm of its own. It is applied inside other formulas and runs whenever the value applying it updates. Its inspector says _Any timing domain_. Leave it there unless it reads a domain-bound value directly."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/timing.md:34
msgid "A **value** — a relationship that reads nothing — usually gets a domain: the sensor's, or the rhythm at which the product should refresh it. A value left on _Any timing domain_ is evaluated whenever any domain ticks (every tick, if the design has no domains at all), which is fine for a small design and imprecise for a real one. An output only accepts a driver that updates in the output's own domain, so a value that drives an output needs that domain."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/timing.md:41
msgid "What happens inside one tick"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/timing.md:43
msgid "Within one tick of a domain, every value in the domain is recomputed from the current inputs. There is no order to choose: the tool works out which value needs which, and evaluates in that order. Two values that need each other _in the same instant_ have no answer — that is an **instantaneous cycle**, reported as _These relationships depend on each other in the same instant: a, b._ The way out is memory."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/timing.md:50
msgid "Remembering last tick's value: `delay`"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/timing.md:56
msgid "`delay(initial, expression)` is the value the expression had **last tick** — and `initial` before there was a last tick. This is how a design holds state: a running total, a previous reading to compare against, a latch. Because the previous value is explicit in the formula, a cycle through a `delay` is not instantaneous and is allowed."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/timing.md:62
msgid "`delay` may be written in a value's formula (a relationship without inputs), at the top level of the formula or inside a `let`, an `if` branch or a `match` scrutinee — not inside a rule that has inputs, and not inside a `match` arm or a block's result. The tool says so if you try."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/timing.md:67
msgid "Reading a value from another domain: `sync`"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/timing.md:69
msgid "If `slowDisplay` (domain _display_) reads `brightness` (domain _interaction_) directly, the tool reports _reads across domains_. The two rhythms are unrelated, so \"the current brightness\" has no meaning in the display's tick."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/timing.md:77
msgid "`sync(domain, initial, expression)` reads the value the expression had at the source domain's **last activation strictly before** this tick, and `initial` before the source has ever activated. The initial value is required because the destination may tick first. The rule \"strictly before\" means a source value produced at the same global instant is not yet visible — you see it on the destination's next tick."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/timing.md:84
msgid "The same idea appears between component instances: connecting a provided port to a required port across domains asks you for a _Starts at_ value and records the transport on the binding ([Carrying a value across timing domains](../workflows/cross-domain-transport.md))."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/timing.md:89
msgid "Why BDL asks for an initial value"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/timing.md:91
msgid "Both `delay` and `sync` are places where a value is read before it has been produced — last tick at tick 0, the source domain before it has run. BDL does not invent a zero: you say what the product should show before the first real value exists, in the destination's own units."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/timing.md:96
msgid "What the simulator shows"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/timing.md:98
msgid "On the Simulate page each domain has a period; the _active_ column of the trace names the domains that ticked. A value whose domain did not activate keeps its cell empty for that tick. Memory and transports show up as values: a `delay` reads its initial value at tick 0, a `sync` reads the source's previous activation. See [Simulate](../studio/simulate.md)."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/timing.md:106
msgid "_For language implementers._ Domains are the kernel's clock environment `Κ`; the per-declaration judgment is `Clocked`, and a direct cross-domain read fails it (`clock.cross_domain_reference`). `delay init e` and `sync src init e` are Core forms with explicit state cells; the tick is a two-phase read/write. `docs/spec/runtime-semantics.md`, `docs/architecture/compiler-pipeline.md` passes 8–10 and 14, DI-17 in `docs/archive/design-issues-ledger.md`. Frequency is deliberately not part of a domain's identity (`docs/spec/kernel.md`)."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/timing.md:116
msgid "[Relationships](relationships.md) · [Simulate](../studio/simulate.md) · [Troubleshooting: timing](../troubleshooting/timing-errors.md) · [Formula language](../reference/formula-language.md)"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:1
msgid "Your first behavior"
msgstr "你的第一个行为"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:3
msgid "**Goal.** A desk lamp whose brightness follows how far its head is tilted: upright is off, flat is full. By the end you will have a design with two concepts, three relationships, one timing domain and one physical output — checked, saved, and ready to [simulate](first-simulation.md)."
msgstr "**目标。** 一盏台灯，亮度随灯头倾斜的角度变化：竖直时熄灭，放平时全亮。完成时你会得到一个包含两个概念、三个关系、一个时序域和一个物理输出的设计——已检查、已保存，可以 [仿真](first-simulation.md)。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:8
msgid "**Time.** About twenty minutes."
msgstr "**用时。** 大约二十分钟。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:10
msgid "You will meet each idea when the design needs it. The [Concepts](../concepts/concepts.md) pages explain each one properly afterwards."
msgstr "每个想法都会在设计需要它时出现。之后 [概念](../concepts/concepts.md) 页面会正式解释每一个。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:13
msgid "1. Create a project"
msgstr "1. 创建项目"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:15
msgid "Launch Studio ([Install and launch](install-and-launch.md))."
msgstr "启动 Studio（[安装与启动](install-and-launch.md)）。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:16
msgid "Click **New Project…**, choose a location and name the folder `lamp`."
msgstr "点击**新建项目…**，选择位置，把文件夹命名为 `lamp`。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:18
msgid "The workspace opens on the **Design** page: a sidebar on the left, an empty canvas in the middle, an inspector on the right, a status line and the page bar along the bottom. The canvas says what to do first: add a concept from the sidebar."
msgstr "工作区在**设计**页打开：左侧是侧栏，中间是空画布，右侧是检查器，底部是状态行和页面栏。画布告诉你先做什么：从侧栏添加一个概念。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:23
msgid "2. Add the two concepts"
msgstr "2. 添加两个概念"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:25
msgid "A **concept** is a value with a meaning. The lamp has two: how far it is tilted, and how bright it is."
msgstr "**概念**是有含义的值。这盏灯有两个：倾斜了多少，以及有多亮。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:28
msgid "In the sidebar's **Project** tab, click **+** next to _Concepts_."
msgstr "在侧栏的**项目**标签页中，点击 _概念_ 旁的 **+**。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:29
msgid "In the _New concept_ sheet: Name `Tilt`. Under _Value_ choose **Quantity**, and for the unit choose **angle** (the symbol `rad` appears in its own column). Click **Create**."
msgstr "在 _新建概念_ 面板中：名称填 `Tilt`。在 _值_ 下选择**量**，单位选择**角度**（符号 `rad` 出现在它自己的一列）。点击**创建**。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:32
msgid "Again **+** next to _Concepts_: Name `Brightness`, **Quantity**, unit **no unit**. Click **Create**."
msgstr "再次点击 _概念_ 旁的 **+**：名称 `Brightness`，**量**，单位**无单位**。点击**创建**。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:35
msgid "Each concept is one row on the canvas with a round socket at each end. The round shape means _quantity_; the colour is the concept's own and will appear wherever _that_ concept is used. Brightness is a quantity with no unit: a level from 0 to 1."
msgstr "每个概念在画布上是一行，两端各有一个圆形插口。圆形表示 _量_；颜色是该概念专属的，凡是用到 _这个_ 概念的地方都会出现。Brightness 是无单位的量：0 到 1 之间的一个水平。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:42
msgid "The sheet previews the row as you type. A hollow ring instead of a filled socket would mean the value form is not chosen yet — that is allowed, and the guide comes back to it."
msgstr "面板会随你输入预览这一行。如果是空心环而不是实心插口，表示值形式尚未选择——这是允许的，指南稍后会回到这一点。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:44
msgid "**What you made.** Two named meanings. Nothing about numbers yet. The sidebar's **Library** tab offers ready-made concepts (_Tilt_ and _Brightness_ are both there); dragging one onto the canvas is the same as filling in the sheet."
msgstr "**你做了什么。** 两个有名字的含义。还没涉及数字。侧栏的**库**标签页提供现成的概念（_Tilt_ 和 _Brightness_ 都在其中）；把一个拖到画布上等同于填写面板。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:48
msgid "3. Add the relationship"
msgstr "3. 添加关系"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:50
msgid "A **relationship** says how one concept follows from others."
msgstr "**关系**说明一个概念如何由其他概念得出。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:52
msgid "Click **+** next to _Mappings_ in the sidebar (the sheet is titled _New mapping_; the guide says _relationship_ — they are the same thing)."
msgstr "点击侧栏中 _映射_ 旁的 **+**（面板标题是 _新建映射_；指南中说 _关系_——它们是同一回事）。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:54
msgid "Name `dimByTilt`. Under _Reads_, switch on **Tilt**. Under _Produces_, choose **Brightness**. Click **Create**."
msgstr "名称 `dimByTilt`。在 _读取_ 下打开 **Tilt**。在 _生成_ 下选择 **Brightness**。点击**创建**。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:57
msgid "A node appears with one input socket (Tilt, on the left) and one output socket (Brightness, on the right). It is drawn **dashed** with the word _declared_ in its header: the relationship exists and has a signature, but no formula yet. That is not an error. You could stop here, save, and come back tomorrow."
msgstr "出现一个节点，有一个输入插口（左侧的 Tilt）和一个输出插口（右侧的 Brightness）。它以**虚线**绘制，标题里写着 _已声明_：关系存在并有签名，但还没有公式。这不是错误。你可以就此停下、保存，明天再回来。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:64
msgid "_A declared relationship: dashed outline and the word declared in its header._"
msgstr "_一个已声明的关系：虚线轮廓，标题中写着“已声明”。_"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:66
msgid "4. Write the formula"
msgstr "4. 写公式"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:68
msgid "Click the `dimByTilt` node. The inspector shows it."
msgstr "点击 `dimByTilt` 节点。检查器会显示它。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:69
msgid "In the **Relationship** section, the editor opens in its **Formula** view: an empty slot, `?`, and the words _produces a Brightness_. Click the slot. Under it, _References_ lists **Tilt** — click it. The slot becomes `Tilt`."
msgstr "在**关系**区，编辑器以**公式**视图打开：一个空槽位 `?`，以及文字 _生成 Brightness_。点击槽位。它下方的 _引用_ 列出了 **Tilt**——点击它。槽位变为 `Tilt`。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:72
msgid "Click `Tilt` and press **÷**. The formula reads `Tilt ÷ ?`, and the new slot is selected: _Expected: an angle, because an angle ÷ an angle = a dimensionless quantity._"
msgstr "点击 `Tilt` 并按 **÷**。公式显示为 `Tilt ÷ ?`，新槽位被选中：_期望：角度，因为角度 ÷ 角度 = 无量纲量。_"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:75
msgid "In the number entry type `90`, choose **deg** from the unit pop-up (only angle units are offered), and press Return. The formula reads `Tilt ÷ 90 deg` and the line under the field says _Valid definition_."
msgstr "在数字输入框中输入 `90`，从单位弹出菜单中选择 **deg**（只提供角度单位），按回车。公式显示为 `Tilt ÷ 90 deg`，字段下方一行显示 _有效的定义_。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:79
msgid "If you would rather type, switch to **Text** and write it as text:"
msgstr "如果你更愿意打字，切换到**文本**并以文本形式写："

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:85
msgid "Both views edit the same formula. Press **⌘↩** or click **Add definition**."
msgstr "两个视图编辑的是同一个公式。按 **⌘↩** 或点击**添加定义**。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:89
#: docs/user-guide/studio/formula-editor.md:18
msgid "_The Formula view with the denominator slot selected: the compiler says the slot expects an angle and why, and offers a number with the angle units, the references that fit and the equations whose result fits._"
msgstr "_选中分母槽位的公式视图：编译器说明该槽位期望角度及原因，并提供带角度单位的数字、合适的引用，以及结果类型合适的方程。_"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:93
msgid "The node now shows its formula in the body and is drawn solid."
msgstr "节点现在在主体中显示公式，并以实线绘制。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:95
msgid "**What you made.** A rule: brightness is the tilt divided by ninety degrees. Try it in the **Text** view: change `90 deg` to `90 s` and watch the line under the field turn red: it says what Brightness is and what the formula produces instead — an angle divided by a time is not a plain number. Put `deg` back. Every formula is checked this way, for units and for meaning, as you type or as you assemble it — and nothing is saved to the design until you press _Add definition_."
msgstr "**你做了什么。** 一条规则：亮度等于倾角除以九十度。在**文本**视图里试试：把 `90 deg` 改成 `90 s`，看字段下方那行变红：它说明 Brightness 是什么，以及公式实际生成的是什么——角度除以时间不是纯数。把 `deg` 改回来。每个公式都会这样检查单位和含义，无论你是打字还是拼装——而且在按下 _添加定义_ 之前，什么都不会保存到设计中。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:105
#: docs/user-guide/studio/formula-editor.md:113
msgid "_The formula field with a draft that does not check: the red verdict line says what Brightness is and what the formula produces instead._"
msgstr "_公式字段中有一个未通过检查的草稿：红色结论行说明 Brightness 是什么，以及公式实际生成的是什么。_"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:110
msgid "In the Text view, **⌃Space** opens completion: the names you can use here (_Tilt_), units after a number, keywords. Hovering a name for a moment shows what it is. The Formula view asks for nothing: each slot lists what fits."
msgstr "在文本视图中，**⌃Space** 打开补全：此处可用的名字（_Tilt_）、数字后的单位、关键字。把鼠标在名字上停留片刻会显示它是什么。公式视图什么都不需要你记：每个槽位都列出适合的内容。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:112
msgid "5. Bring the tilt in from the environment"
msgstr "5. 把倾角从环境引进来"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:114
msgid "`dimByTilt` is a rule, not a value: it needs a tilt to work on. Where does the tilt come from? From the environment — a sensor, outside the design. In BDL a value the environment provides is a **Source**: a relationship that **reads nothing**, produces the concept, and has **no formula**."
msgstr "`dimByTilt` 是规则，不是值：它需要一个倾角来处理。倾角从哪里来？来自环境——设计之外的一个传感器。在 BDL 中，由环境提供的值是一个**来源**：一个**不读取任何东西**、生成该概念、并且**没有公式**的关系。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:119
msgid "**+** next to _Mappings_: Name `tilt`, read nothing, produce **Tilt**. Create. (Right-click the canvas → **Add Source ▸** → _New source…_ makes the same thing; the Library's _Sources_ section makes a concept and its Source together.)"
msgstr "点击 _映射_ 旁的 **+**：名称 `tilt`，不读取任何东西，生成 **Tilt**。创建。（右键点击画布 → **添加来源 ▸** → _新建来源…_ 会做出同样的东西；库的 _来源_ 分区会同时做出一个概念和它的来源。）"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:124
msgid "The node says _Source_ in its header, with a bar down its left edge and no input socket. It is not dashed: nothing is missing. In the simulator you will type its value; on a device the sensor will provide it."
msgstr "节点的标题写着 _来源_，左边缘有一条竖条，没有输入插口。它不是虚线的：这里没有任何缺失。在仿真器中你将输入它的值；在设备上由传感器提供。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:128
msgid "6. Compute the lamp's brightness"
msgstr "6. 计算灯的亮度"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:130
msgid "The value the lamp actually shows is `dimByTilt` applied to `tilt`. That is again a relationship that reads nothing and produces Brightness — this time with a formula."
msgstr "灯实际显示的值是把 `dimByTilt` 应用于 `tilt`。这又是一个不读取任何东西、生成 Brightness 的关系——这次带有公式。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:134
msgid "**+** next to _Mappings_: Name `brightness`, read nothing, produce **Brightness**. Create."
msgstr "点击 _映射_ 旁的 **+**：名称 `brightness`，不读取任何东西，生成 **Brightness**。创建。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:136
msgid "Select it and enter the formula `dimByTilt(tilt)`. _Add definition._"
msgstr "选中它并输入公式 `dimByTilt(tilt)`。_添加定义。_"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:138
msgid "Completion offers `dimByTilt(` because it is a relationship with an input, and `tilt` because it is a value. The formula field is the only place where relationships are combined; links on the canvas show _which concepts_ a relationship reads, not the arithmetic."
msgstr "补全会提供 `dimByTilt(`，因为它是带输入的关系；也会提供 `tilt`，因为它是值。公式字段是唯一组合关系的地方；画布上的连线显示关系读取 _哪些概念_，而不是算术。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:143
msgid "**What you made.** Three relationships: a Source (`tilt`), a rule (`dimByTilt`) and a computed value (`brightness`). The status line at the bottom counts them."
msgstr "**你做了什么。** 三个关系：一个来源（`tilt`）、一条规则（`dimByTilt`）和一个计算值（`brightness`）。底部的状态行会计数。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:146
msgid "7. Give the values a rhythm"
msgstr "7. 给值一个节奏"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:148
msgid "A value that comes from outside has a rhythm: the sensor reports every so often. In BDL that rhythm is a named **timing domain**, and every value that updates on its own belongs to one."
msgstr "来自外部的值有节奏：传感器每隔一段时间报告一次。在 BDL 中，这个节奏是一个有名字的**时序域**，每个自行更新的值都属于某一个。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:152
msgid "**+** next to _Timing domains_: name it `interaction`. Create."
msgstr "点击 _时序域_ 旁的 **+**：命名为 `interaction`。创建。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:153
msgid "Select `tilt`. In the inspector's **Timing** section, set **Updates in** to _interaction_."
msgstr "选中 `tilt`。在检查器的**时序**区，把**更新于**设为 _interaction_。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:155
msgid "Select `brightness` and do the same."
msgstr "选中 `brightness`，做同样的事。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:157
msgid "`dimByTilt` stays on _Any timing domain_: it is a pure rule and takes the rhythm of whatever applies it. The domain's name appears quietly at the right edge of the two nodes."
msgstr "`dimByTilt` 保持在 _任意时序域_：它是纯规则，跟随应用它的那一方的节奏。域的名字安静地出现在两个节点的右边缘。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:161
msgid "**What you made.** A design in which \"when does this update\" is an explicit decision. A domain is a name, not a rate — how often _interaction_ ticks is chosen when you simulate or deploy, not here."
msgstr "**你做了什么。** 一个把“这个什么时候更新”作为显式决定的设计。域是名字，不是速率——_interaction_ 多久走一拍是在仿真或部署时选择的，不在这里。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:165
msgid "8. Add the light"
msgstr "8. 添加灯"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:167
msgid "Brightness is a value inside the design. The lamp itself is a **physical output**: the place where a value leaves the design for the world."
msgstr "Brightness 是设计内部的值。灯本身是一个**物理输出**：值离开设计、进入世界的地方。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:170
msgid "**+** next to _Outputs_. In the _New output_ sheet: Name `light`, **Accepts** Brightness, **Updates in** interaction, **Required** on. Create."
msgstr "点击 _输出_ 旁的 **+**。在 _新建输出_ 面板中：名称 `light`，**接受** Brightness，**更新于** interaction，打开**必需**。创建。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:173
msgid "A sink node appears at the right edge of the canvas, drawn dashed: it has a domain but nothing drives it yet. The status line says _outputs incomplete_."
msgstr "画布右边缘出现一个汇节点，以虚线绘制：它有域，但还没有东西驱动它。状态行显示 _输出未完成_。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:176
msgid "Drag from `brightness`'s output socket onto the sink's socket. (Or select the output and pick `brightness` in the **Connect** pop-up of its inspector; the pop-up marks relationships that _have inputs_, which cannot drive an output.)"
msgstr "从 `brightness` 的输出插口拖到汇节点的插口上。（或者选中输出，在其检查器的**连接**弹出菜单中选择 `brightness`；弹出菜单会标记 _有输入_ 的关系，它们不能驱动输出。）"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:180
msgid "The sink becomes solid. Only a relationship that _reads nothing_ and produces the accepted concept in the same domain can drive an output. `brightness` qualifies; connecting `dimByTilt` instead would be accepted as an edit and then reported under the output as a connection that does not fit."
msgstr "汇节点变为实线。只有 _不读取任何东西_、并在同一域中生成所接受概念的关系才能驱动输出。`brightness` 符合条件；如果改连 `dimByTilt`，编辑会被接受，然后在输出下方被报告为不合适的连接。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:185
msgid "**What you made.** A complete design. The status line no longer says _outputs incomplete_, and nothing is _not yet defined_: `tilt`, the Source, is meant to stay without a formula, and the line counts it as _1 source_. Press **⌘S** to save."
msgstr "**你做了什么。** 一个完整的设计。状态行不再显示 _输出未完成_，也没有任何 _尚未定义_ 的项：来源 `tilt` 本来就应该没有公式，状态行把它计为 _1 个来源_。按 **⌘S** 保存。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:190
msgid "What you have"
msgstr "你现在拥有的"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:194
msgid "_The finished lamp: the Source tilt, the rule dimByTilt, the value brightness, and the driven light._"
msgstr "_完成的灯：来源 tilt、规则 dimByTilt、值 brightness，以及被驱动的 light。_"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:197
msgid "Object"
msgstr "对象"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:197
msgid "Kind"
msgstr "种类"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:197
msgid "Updates in"
msgstr "更新于"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:199
msgid "**Tilt**"
msgstr "**Tilt**"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:199
msgid "concept, an angle"
msgstr "概念，角度"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:200
msgid "**Brightness**"
msgstr "**Brightness**"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:200
msgid "concept, a plain number"
msgstr "概念，纯数"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:201
msgid "**tilt**"
msgstr "**tilt**"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:201
msgid "relationship reading nothing: a Source"
msgstr "不读取任何东西的关系：来源"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:201
msgid "_none_"
msgstr "_无_"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:201
#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:203
#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:204
msgid "_interaction_"
msgstr "_interaction_"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:202
msgid "**dimByTilt**"
msgstr "**dimByTilt**"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:202
msgid "relationship reading Tilt: a rule"
msgstr "读取 Tilt 的关系：规则"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:202
msgid "`Tilt / 90 deg`"
msgstr "`Tilt / 90 deg`"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:202
#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:13
msgid "any"
msgstr "任意"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:203
msgid "**brightness**"
msgstr "**brightness**"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:203
msgid "relationship reading nothing: a value"
msgstr "不读取任何东西的关系：值"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:203
#: docs/user-guide/textual/syntax-basics.md:166
msgid "`dimByTilt(tilt)`"
msgstr "`dimByTilt(tilt)`"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:204
msgid "**light**"
msgstr "**light**"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:204
msgid "physical output driven by brightness"
msgstr "由 brightness 驱动的物理输出"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:206
msgid "The design is _executable_: every relationship the output depends on is defined or is a Source, checks, has a rhythm, and the output has exactly one driver."
msgstr "这个设计是 _可执行的_：输出所依赖的每个关系要么已定义要么是来源，通过检查，有节奏，并且输出恰好有一个驱动方。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:209
#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:83
#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:83
msgid "If something does not work"
msgstr "如果有什么不对"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:211
msgid "**The formula line is red.** Read it: it names the problem in terms of your concepts (\"this divides an angle by a time\"). See [Types, units and concepts](../troubleshooting/type-and-concept-errors.md)."
msgstr "**公式行是红色的。** 读一读：它用你的概念来说明问题（“这把角度除以了时间”）。见 [类型、单位与概念](../troubleshooting/type-and-concept-errors.md)。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:214
msgid "**`brightness` will not connect to the output.** Check its _Updates in_ matches the output's, and that it reads nothing. See [Connections](../troubleshooting/connection-errors.md)."
msgstr "**`brightness` 连不上输出。** 检查它的 _更新于_ 是否与输出一致，以及它是否不读取任何东西。见 [连接](../troubleshooting/connection-errors.md)。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:217
msgid "**The status line says _N definitions not added_.** A formula is typed but not added; select the node and press _Add definition_ or _Revert_."
msgstr "**状态行显示 _N 个定义未添加_。** 公式已输入但未添加；选中节点，按 _添加定义_ 或 _还原_。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:219
msgid "**Nothing checks and the bottom line says _Compiler not connected_.** See [Install and launch](install-and-launch.md)."
msgstr "**什么都不检查，底部一行显示 _编译器未连接_。** 见 [安装与启动](install-and-launch.md)。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:222
#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:93
#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:96
#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:71
#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/what-is-bdl.md:77
#: docs/user-guide/textual/overview.md:124
#: docs/user-guide/workflows/authoring-as-text.md:109
#: docs/user-guide/workflows/composing-components.md:67
#: docs/user-guide/workflows/grouping-behavior.md:69
#: docs/user-guide/workflows/package-as-component.md:71
msgid "Next"
msgstr "下一步"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-behavior.md:224
msgid "[Your first simulation](first-simulation.md) — tilt the lamp and watch the brightness."
msgstr "[你的第一次仿真](first-simulation.md)——倾斜灯，观察亮度。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:1
msgid "Your first deployment check"
msgstr "你的第一次部署检查"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:3
msgid "**Goal.** Find out whether the lamp from the [first tutorial](first-behavior.md) fits an Arduino Nano — and see what \"does not fit\" looks like."
msgstr "**目标。** 弄清 [第一个教程](first-behavior.md) 中的灯能否放进 Arduino Nano——并看看“放不下”是什么样子。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:6
#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:6
msgid "**Time.** Ten minutes."
msgstr "**用时。** 十分钟。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:8
msgid "Deployment in Behavior Designer today means _checking placement_: which board pin each physical output's device would use, or why none can. It does not build firmware or flash a board yet."
msgstr "今天 Behavior Designer 中的部署指的是 _检查布置_：每个物理输出的设备会用板子的哪个引脚，或者为什么没有引脚可用。它还不会构建固件或烧录板子。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:12
msgid "1. Open the Deploy page"
msgstr "1. 打开部署页"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:14
msgid "Click **Deploy** in the page bar (or **⌘3**). On the left, a **Target** pop-up and a **Devices** list; in the middle, the verdict for the chosen board."
msgstr "点击页面栏中的**部署**（或 **⌘3**）。左侧是**目标板**弹出菜单和**设备**列表；中间是所选板子的结论。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:17
msgid "Until you choose a board the page says _Choose a board to see whether this design fits it._"
msgstr "在你选择板子之前，页面显示 _选择一块板子，看这个设计能否放进去。_"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:20
msgid "2. Choose a board"
msgstr "2. 选择板子"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:22
msgid "In **Target**, choose **Arduino Nano**. The verdict reads:"
msgstr "在**目标板**中选择 **Arduino Nano**。结论显示："

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:24
msgid "Fits Arduino Nano so far — the binding is not finished."
msgstr "目前能放进 Arduino Nano——绑定尚未完成。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:26
msgid "and under it: _No device on arduino_nano for: light._ (this line names the board by its short id). The design has an output but nothing says what piece of hardware realises it."
msgstr "其下：_arduino_nano 上没有对应的设备：light。_（这一行用板子的短 id 称呼它）。设计有一个输出，但没有说明哪件硬件实现它。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:30
msgid "3. Add a device"
msgstr "3. 添加设备"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:32
msgid "A **device** is the hardware that realises one output on the board: a PWM channel for a dimmable light, a digital output for a relay, an H-bridge for a motor."
msgstr "**设备**是在板子上实现一个输出的硬件：可调光灯用 PWM 通道，继电器用数字输出，电机用 H 桥。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:36
msgid "Click **Add device**. A row appears in _Devices_."
msgstr "点击**添加设备**。_设备_ 中出现一行。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:37
msgid "Name it `pwmLight`. In its kind pop-up choose **PWM channel**. In its output pop-up choose **light**."
msgstr "命名为 `pwmLight`。在它的种类弹出菜单中选择 **PWM 通道**。在它的输出弹出菜单中选择 **light**。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:40
msgid "The verdict changes to **Feasible on Arduino Nano.** and a _Placement on arduino_nano_ table shows the one line the lamp needs: `pwmLight`, its _PWM_ requirement, and the pin it was given, such as `D3`."
msgstr "结论变为**可部署到 Arduino Nano。**，并且 _arduino_nano 上的布置_ 表格显示这盏灯需要的那一行：`pwmLight`、它的 _PWM_ 需求，以及分配给它的引脚，例如 `D3`。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:44
msgid "**What you made.** A deployment configuration for one board. It lives in the project with the design, but it is a separate layer: the Design page's verdicts did not change when you added the device, and they will not change if you pick another board."
msgstr "**你做了什么。** 一块板子的部署配置。它和设计一起保存在项目中，但是独立的一层：添加设备时设计页的结论没有变，换另一块板子它们也不会变。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:51
#: docs/user-guide/studio/deploy.md:12
msgid "_The Deploy page: Arduino Nano chosen, one PWM device on light, the verdict and the placement._"
msgstr "_部署页：选中 Arduino Nano，light 上有一个 PWM 设备，以及结论和布置。_"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:54
msgid "4. Make it fail on purpose"
msgstr "4. 故意让它失败"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:56
msgid "Each device row has one pin field per requirement. In `pwmLight`'s pin field type `D4` — a pin that cannot do PWM on the Nano."
msgstr "每个设备行的每个需求都有一个引脚栏。在 `pwmLight` 的引脚栏输入 `D4`——Nano 上一个不能做 PWM 的引脚。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:59
msgid "Not feasible on Arduino Nano."
msgstr "无法部署到 Arduino Nano。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:62
msgid " D4 cannot carry pwmLight PWM on arduino_nano. The pin chosen by hand, D4, cannot carry pwmLight PWM here."
msgstr " 在 arduino_nano 上 D4 无法承载 pwmLight 的 PWM。手动选择的引脚 D4 在这里无法承载 pwmLight 的 PWM。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:64
msgid "Clear the field: feasible again. Now switch **Target** to **Big board (mock)**: feasible there too, on a different pin. Switch back."
msgstr "清空该栏：又可部署了。现在把**目标板**切换到 **Big board (mock)**：那里也可部署，只是引脚不同。再切回来。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:67
msgid "**What happened.** Feasibility is a fact about _this design on this board_. The board choice is a session preference — it is not saved with the project — and the placement is recomputed for whatever board is chosen."
msgstr "**发生了什么。** 可部署性是关于 _这个设计在这块板子上_ 的事实。板子的选择是会话偏好——不随项目保存——布置会针对所选的任何板子重新计算。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:73
msgid "_Not feasible: the pin chosen by hand cannot carry PWM._"
msgstr "_无法部署：手动选择的引脚无法承载 PWM。_"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:75
msgid "What \"feasible\" means, and does not"
msgstr "“可部署”意味着什么，不意味着什么"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:77
msgid "_Feasible_ means every device's requirements can be placed on distinct pins with the right capabilities. It does not mean the circuit will work electrically: current, voltage and timing resolution are not modelled. When several placements are possible the tool shows one; when none is, it shows the first dead end it hit, which is _a_ conflict, not necessarily the only one."
msgstr "_可部署_ 意味着每个设备的需求都能放到具备相应能力的、互不相同的引脚上。它不意味着电路在电气上能工作：电流、电压和时序分辨率没有建模。当有多种布置可能时，工具显示其中一种；当一种都没有时，它显示遇到的第一个死路，那是 _一个_ 冲突，不一定是唯一的。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:85
msgid "**The status line still says _not causal_ or _outputs incomplete_.** The Deploy verdict is only about the board; the design itself is not ready. Fix it on the Design page first. See [Deployment](../troubleshooting/deployment-errors.md)."
msgstr "**状态行仍然显示 _存在瞬时环路_ 或 _输出未完成_。** 部署结论只关乎板子；设计本身还没准备好。先在设计页修好它。见 [部署](../troubleshooting/deployment-errors.md)。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:89
msgid "**Not connected to an output: …** — a device with no output chosen."
msgstr "**未连接到输出：…**——一个没有选择输出的设备。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:90
msgid "**Nothing on Arduino Nano can carry …** — the board has no free pin with that capability; try another kind of device, another board, or fewer devices."
msgstr "**Arduino Nano 上没有东西能承载 …**——板子上没有具备该能力的空闲引脚；试试另一种设备、另一块板子，或更少的设备。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-deployment.md:95
msgid "You have built, simulated and placed a behavior. Read the [Concepts](../concepts/concepts.md) pages for the ideas you used, or go straight to [From sensor to output](../workflows/sensor-to-output.md) to extend the lamp with an ambient-light sensor."
msgstr "你已经搭建、仿真并布置了一个行为。阅读 [概念](../concepts/concepts.md) 页面了解你用到的想法，或者直接去 [从传感器到输出](../workflows/sensor-to-output.md)，给灯加上环境光传感器。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:1
msgid "Your first simulation"
msgstr "你的第一次仿真"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:3
msgid "**Goal.** Tilt the lamp from the [first tutorial](first-behavior.md) and watch its brightness, one tick at a time."
msgstr "**目标。** 倾斜 [第一个教程](first-behavior.md) 中的灯，一拍一拍地观察它的亮度。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:8
msgid "1. Open the Simulate page"
msgstr "1. 打开仿真页"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:10
msgid "Click **Simulate** in the page bar at the bottom (or press **⌘2**)."
msgstr "点击底部页面栏中的**仿真**（或按 **⌘2**）。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:12
msgid "The page has three parts:"
msgstr "这个页面有三个部分："

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:14
msgid "**Sources**, on the left — one control for every value the environment provides. Here that is `tilt`, with a number field and the unit `rad` beside it. Under the Sources, **Timing domains** lists `interaction` with a period: _every 1_ tick."
msgstr "左侧的**来源**——每个由环境提供的值一个控件。这里是 `tilt`，一个数字栏，旁边是单位 `rad`。来源下方，**时序域**列出了 `interaction` 及其周期：_每 1_ 拍。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:18
msgid "the **trace**, in the middle — a table that fills as you step: one row per tick, a column for every computed value and every driven output. Above it, **Step**, **Step ×10** and **Reset**, and the tick counter."
msgstr "中间的**轨迹**——随你步进而填充的表格：每拍一行，每个计算值和每个被驱动的输出一列。上方是**步进**、**步进 ×10** 和**重置**，以及拍计数器。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:21
msgid "the **Probe**, on the right — the value of whatever is selected, now and over the run."
msgstr "右侧的**探针**——当前选中对象的值，包括现在的值和整个运行中的值。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:24
msgid "Nothing runs until you step. If anything in the design would stop a step, it is listed above the trace as a sentence about the object — _tilt needs a value before simulation can step._ — with a _Show_ link that selects it. Step is disabled while such a line is there."
msgstr "在你步进之前什么都不会运行。如果设计中有任何东西会阻止步进，它会在轨迹上方以一句关于该对象的话列出——_tilt 需要一个值仿真才能步进。_——并附有一个 _显示_ 链接来选中它。只要有这样一行，步进就被禁用。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:29
msgid "2. Give the tilt a value"
msgstr "2. 给倾角一个值"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:31
msgid "In the `tilt` field enter `0.7854` (45°; the field takes the base unit shown beside it — radians for an angle)."
msgstr "在 `tilt` 栏输入 `0.7854`（45°；该栏使用旁边显示的基本单位——角度用弧度）。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:34
msgid "3. Step"
msgstr "3. 步进"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:36
msgid "Click **Step**."
msgstr "点击**步进**。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:38
msgid "The trace gains its first row: tick 0, the active domain _interaction_, the Source as the evaluator read it — `tilt` as `Tilt(0.785398 [rad])` — and the values the design computed — `brightness` as `Brightness(0.5)` (or within a few digits of it, depending on what you typed), and the _light_ column showing the same value, because `brightness` drives it. A value is always written with the concept it belongs to. Click **Step** twice more: three rows, the same values, because the Source has not changed."
msgstr "轨迹得到第一行：第 0 拍，活动域 _interaction_，求值器读到的来源——`tilt` 为 `Tilt(0.785398 [rad])`——以及设计计算出的值——`brightness` 为 `Brightness(0.5)`（或者相差几位小数，取决于你输入的值），_light_ 列显示同样的值，因为 `brightness` 驱动它。值总是和它所属的概念一起书写。再点两次**步进**：三行，同样的值，因为来源没变。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:46
msgid "Change the field to `1.5708` (90°) and **Step**: about `Brightness(1)`. Set `0` and step: `Brightness(0)`. Upright is off; flat is full."
msgstr "把栏改为 `1.5708`（90°）并**步进**：约为 `Brightness(1)`。设为 `0` 再步进：`Brightness(0)`。竖直时熄灭，放平时全亮。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:49
msgid "**What happened.** Each tick, every value in the _interaction_ domain was recomputed from the inputs you supplied. The evaluator that produced these numbers is the one that defines what a BDL design means; the generated code for a device is held to it."
msgstr "**发生了什么。** 每一拍，_interaction_ 域中的每个值都根据你提供的输入重新计算。产生这些数字的求值器就是定义 BDL 设计含义的那个；为设备生成的代码必须与之一致。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:54
#: docs/user-guide/studio/simulate.md:9
msgid "![The Simulate page: on the left, under Sources, a control for tilt showing 0.785398 rad and the interaction domain's period of every 1 ticks; in the middle the Step, Step ×10 and Reset buttons, tick 3, and a trace with three rows whose tilt, brightness and light columns read Tilt(0.785398 [rad]), Brightness(0.5) and Brightness(0.5); on the right the probe for brightness with Brightness(0.5) now and at each tick over the run.](../assets/studio/simulate-page.png)"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:56
#: docs/user-guide/studio/simulate.md:11
msgid "_The Simulate page after three steps with the tilt at 45°: the Sources on the left, the trace in the middle, the probe on the right._"
msgstr "_倾角为 45° 时步进三次后的仿真页：左侧是来源，中间是轨迹，右侧是探针。_"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:59
msgid "4. Look at one value"
msgstr "4. 查看一个值"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:61
msgid "Click the `brightness` column header, or select `brightness` on the Design page and come back. The **Probe** shows its value now and its values over the run, written as in the trace, with the concept's glyph. Open **Explain** under it for the formal detail — the identity number and the run's revision."
msgstr "点击 `brightness` 列标题，或在设计页上选中 `brightness` 再回来。**探针**显示它现在的值和整个运行中的值，写法与轨迹中相同，带有概念的图形符号。展开其下的**解释**可查看形式化细节——标识号和运行的修订号。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:66
msgid "5. Reset and try the rhythm"
msgstr "5. 重置并试试节奏"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:68
msgid "**Reset** returns to tick 0 and keeps your inputs."
msgstr "**重置**回到第 0 拍并保留你的输入。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:70
msgid "Under _Timing domains_, set _interaction_ to _every 2_. **Step ×10**: the _active_ column now names _interaction_ only on every second tick, and `tilt`'s cell is shown only on those ticks — on the others the domain did not activate, so no value was read. A period is a simulation choice; the design itself only says _which_ domain a value belongs to."
msgstr "在 _时序域_ 下，把 _interaction_ 设为 _每 2_。**步进 ×10**：_活动_ 列现在只在每隔一拍时写着 _interaction_，`tilt` 的单元格也只在那些拍显示——其余拍该域没有激活，所以没有读取任何值。周期是仿真的选择；设计本身只说明值属于 _哪个_ 域。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:76
msgid "What a step actually does"
msgstr "一次步进实际做了什么"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:78
msgid "Every step is a replay: the simulator restarts at tick 0 with all the inputs you have entered so far and runs to the new tick. The same design, the same inputs and the same periods give the same trace, every time. Changing the design on the Design page drops the trace; your input values stay."
msgstr "每次步进都是重放：仿真器带着你迄今输入的所有值从第 0 拍重新开始，运行到新的一拍。同样的设计、同样的输入和同样的周期每次都给出同样的轨迹。在设计页上修改设计会丢弃轨迹；你的输入值保留。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:85
msgid "**Step is disabled and a sentence names a relationship.** Read it: a Source without a value, a concept without a value form, a relationship without a valid definition, or relationships that depend on each other in the same instant. Each has a _Show_ link. See [Incomplete design](../troubleshooting/incomplete-design.md)."
msgstr "**步进被禁用，并有一句话指出某个关系。** 读一读：没有值的来源、没有值形式的概念、没有有效定义的关系，或者在同一瞬间相互依赖的关系。每一条都有 _显示_ 链接。见 [未完成的设计](../troubleshooting/incomplete-design.md)。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:90
msgid "**A tick stops with a message on the controls' line** (for example a division by zero). The message names the relationship. Change the formula or the inputs and step again."
msgstr "**某一拍停止，控件行上出现消息**（例如除以零）。消息会指出关系。修改公式或输入，再次步进。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:93
msgid "**The trace is empty after you edited the design.** Expected — the run belongs to one version of the design. Step again."
msgstr "**编辑设计后轨迹为空。** 这是预期的——运行属于设计的某一个版本。再次步进。"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/first-simulation.md:98
msgid "[Your first deployment check](first-deployment.md) — does this lamp fit an Arduino Nano?"
msgstr "[你的第一次部署检查](first-deployment.md)——这盏灯能放进 Arduino Nano 吗？"

#: docs/user-guide/getting-started/install-and-launch.md:1
msgid "Install and launch"
