#: docs/user-guide/studio/workspace.md:47
msgid "The button at the left of the page bar (⊞) closes the project and returns to the project manager. The gear at the right opens **Preferences…**: the language Studio speaks (System Default, English, 简体中文, 日本語), which changes only what Studio shows — never the BDL source, the project files or the compiler. The same link is on the project manager."
msgstr "页面栏左侧的按钮（⊞）关闭项目并返回项目管理器。右侧的齿轮打开**偏好设置…**：Studio 使用的语言（跟随系统、English、简体中文、日本語），它只改变 Studio 显示的内容——从不改变 BDL 源码、项目文件或编译器。项目管理器上也有同样的链接。"

#: docs/user-guide/studio/workspace.md:53
msgid "Saving, undo, revisions"
msgstr "保存、撤销、修订"

#: docs/user-guide/studio/workspace.md:55
msgid "**⌘S** or **Save** writes the whole project to its folder — the design, the layout, and every unfinished edit: a formula typed and not added, text in the Code view that does not build yet. A design change is recorded as a new _revision_ of the project; **⌘Z** / **⇧⌘Z** step through them. Moving nodes, resizing panels and collapsing groups are not design changes: they are saved but make no revision. A typed formula that has not been added is a _draft_ — it is kept when you switch selection or pages, saved with the project, and the status line counts it as _definition not added_ until you add or revert it."
msgstr "**⌘S** 或**保存**把整个项目写入它的文件夹——设计、布局，以及每一个未完成的编辑：已输入但未添加的公式、代码视图中尚不能构建的文本。设计改动会记录为项目的一个新 _修订_；**⌘Z** / **⇧⌘Z** 在它们之间前后移动。移动节点、调整面板大小和折叠分组不是设计改动：它们会被保存，但不产生修订。已输入但未添加的公式是一份 _草稿_——切换选择或页面时会保留，随项目一起保存，在你添加或还原之前，状态行把它计为 _定义未添加_。"

#: docs/user-guide/studio/workspace.md:64
msgid "Closing a project"
msgstr "关闭项目"

#: docs/user-guide/studio/workspace.md:66
msgid "**Close**, the project manager button (⊞), **⌘W**, **⌘Q**, the menu's Quit, the window's close button, and opening or creating another project all ask the same question when the project differs from what is saved:"
msgstr "**关闭**、项目管理器按钮（⊞）、**⌘W**、**⌘Q**、菜单中的退出、窗口的关闭按钮，以及打开或创建另一个项目，在项目与已保存内容不同时都会问同一个问题："

#: docs/user-guide/studio/workspace.md:70
msgid "Save changes to “lamp”? **Don't Save** · **Cancel** · **Save**"
msgstr "是否保存对“lamp”的更改？**不保存** · **取消** · **保存**"

#: docs/user-guide/studio/workspace.md:72
msgid "**Save** saves everything as it is now and then closes; if the save is refused (a file changed on disk — see the banner), the project stays open. **Don't Save** closes; the next open returns to what was last saved. **Cancel** (Esc) changes nothing. A project that is _Saved_ closes at once. Nothing asks twice, and nothing closes while the question is open."
msgstr "**保存**原样保存一切然后关闭；如果保存被拒绝（有文件在磁盘上被修改——见横幅），项目保持打开。**不保存**直接关闭；下次打开回到上次保存的状态。**取消**（Esc）什么都不改。_已保存_ 的项目立即关闭。不会问两次，问题未回答时也不会关闭任何东西。"

#: docs/user-guide/studio/workspace.md:78
msgid "The three levels of information"
msgstr "三个信息层次"

#: docs/user-guide/studio/workspace.md:80
msgid "Studio shows a design at three levels, and keeps them apart:"
msgstr "Studio 在三个层次上展示设计，并把它们分开："

#: docs/user-guide/studio/workspace.md:82
msgid "**Canvas** — structure you can see: shape, colour, links, dashed outlines, a red mark. No type names, no identifiers."
msgstr "**画布**——看得见的结构：形状、颜色、连线、虚线轮廓、红色标记。没有类型名，没有标识符。"

#: docs/user-guide/studio/workspace.md:84
msgid "**Inspector** — designer vocabulary: _Meaning_, _Value_, _Reads_, _Produces_, _Updates in_, _Drives_; findings in product language beside the field they concern."
msgstr "**检查器**——设计师的词汇：_含义_、_值_、_读取_、_生成_、_更新于_、_驱动_；用产品语言写的发现项，紧挨着它们涉及的字段。"

#: docs/user-guide/studio/workspace.md:87
msgid "**Explain** — a collapsed disclosure at the end of every inspector: the identity numbers, the formal interface and terms, diagnostic codes, the revision. Nothing in the first two levels depends on it."
msgstr "**解释**——每个检查器末尾一个折叠的展开区：标识号、形式化接口和项、诊断代码、修订号。前两个层次没有任何东西依赖它。"

#: docs/user-guide/studio/workspace.md:91
msgid "This guide follows the same order: it explains the canvas and the inspector, and points to _Explain_ and the technical documentation for the rest."
msgstr "本指南遵循同样的顺序：解释画布和检查器，其余的指向 _解释_ 和技术文档。"

#: docs/user-guide/studio/workspace.md:96
msgid "[Canvas](canvas.md) · [Library](library.md) · [Inspector](inspector.md) · [Keyboard and mouse](../reference/keyboard-and-mouse.md)"
msgstr "[画布](canvas.md) · [库](library.md) · [检查器](inspector.md) · [键盘与鼠标](../reference/keyboard-and-mouse.md)"

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:1
msgid "Editor and language server"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:3
msgid "`bdl-lsp` is a language server for `.bdl` files. It speaks the Language Server Protocol over standard input and output, so any editor with LSP support can use it. A reference VS Code extension is in `editors/vscode` (see its README); for other editors you configure the client to launch the binary."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:8
msgid "Launching"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:10
msgid "Build it with the rest of the workspace (`cargo build --workspace`, or `just build`); the binary is `target/debug/bdl-lsp`. Run it with no arguments; it logs to standard error (set `RUST_LOG` to change the level)."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:14
msgid "Point your editor's LSP client at that binary for files with the `.bdl` extension. In VS Code, install the extension from `editors/vscode` and set `bdl.serverPath` to the binary."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:18
msgid "Which project it works on"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:20
msgid "At start-up the server looks for a **project root** — a folder containing `bdl.toml`:"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:23
msgid "`initializationOptions.projectRoot`, if your client sends it (the VS Code extension sends the nearest such folder above the active file);"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:25
msgid "otherwise the first workspace folder;"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:26
msgid "otherwise the older `rootUri`."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:28
msgid "**The project** (sources under `src/`) is the workspace: every `src/**/*.bdl` file is known to the server whether or not you have it open, and every answer is about the whole project — a definition in another file, references across files, a rename that touches three files. An open buffer replaces the file on disk while it is open; nothing is written by the server except the identity sidecar (`.bdl/identities.json`) after a save or an outside change, so the next tool to open the project agrees on identities. Saving is the editor's ordinary save of the `.bdl` file."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:37
msgid "**A project saved by an older version of Studio** (a `design/*.json` file, no `src/`) is converted to `.bdl` sources the first time any tool opens it, the language server included; from then on it is an ordinary workspace."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:41
msgid "**No project**: the server starts empty and open documents alone populate it."
msgstr ""

